          "content": {
            "size": 34495,
            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "compression": 26985,
            "text": "{\"priorities\":[{\"id\":\"every-change-that-reaches-the-build-fleet-is-verified-before-a-person-reads-it\",\"title\":\"Every change that reaches the build fleet is verified before a person reads it\",\"description\":\"Every change that reaches the build fleet is verified before a person is asked to read it, so a reviewer opens work that already builds, passes its checks and says what it proves.\\n\\nThe work under it is the verification run each change starts, the record it leaves beside the change, and the pages both review layers read, from [the priorities page](/priorities). It is finished when no reviewer reads a change whose checks have not run, and when a check that failed says which line of the change it read.\",\"description_tree\":{\"type\":\"doc\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Every change that reaches the build fleet is verified before a person is asked to read it, so a reviewer opens work that already builds, passes its checks and says what it proves.\"}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The work under it is the verification run each change starts, the record it leaves beside the change, and the pages both review layers read, from \"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"the priorities page\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"link\",\"attrs\":{\"href\":\"/priorities\"}}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\". It is finished when no reviewer reads a change whose checks have not run, and when a check that failed says which line of the change it read.\"}]}]},\"description_tree_exact\":true,\"owner\":\"Verify's, Fleet's and Release's controllers\",\"rank\":\"U\",\"state\":\"live\",\"made_at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.415095Z\",\"made_by\":{\"kind\":\"user\",\"id\":\"alice\",\"proven\":true},\"work\":{\"by_status\":{\"backlog\":1,\"done\":0,\"icebox\":1,\"in_progress\":6,\"needs_review\":1,\"retro\":1,\"testing\":2,\"todo\":4,\"triage\":2},\"claimed\":4,\"open_asks\":2,\"closed_last_7_days\":0,\"newest_event_at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:10.669378Z\"}},{\"id\":\"docs-refresh\",\"title\":\"Docs refresh\",\"description\":\"The docs site says what the product does today, in the words a new reader looks for. Each page names the version it was checked against, and a page nobody has checked in a quarter says so at its top rather than reading as current. The work is a pass over every page, a check that fails the docs build when a page names a command that no longer exists, and a short list of the pages readers open most, which are read first.\",\"description_tree\":{\"type\":\"doc\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The docs site says what the product does today, in the words a new reader looks for. Each page names the version it was checked against, and a page nobody has checked in a quarter says so at its top rather than reading as current. The work is a pass over every page, a check that fails the docs build when a page names a command that no longer exists, and a short list of the pages readers open most, which are read first.\"}]}]},\"description_tree_exact\":true,\"owner\":\"alice\",\"rank\":\"V\",\"state\":\"live\",\"made_at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.419834Z\",\"made_by\":{\"kind\":\"user\",\"id\":\"alice\",\"proven\":true},\"work\":{\"by_status\":{\"backlog\":0,\"done\":0,\"icebox\":0,\"in_progress\":0,\"needs_review\":0,\"retro\":0,\"testing\":0,\"todo\":1,\"triage\":1},\"claimed\":0,\"open_asks\":1,\"closed_last_7_days\":0,\"newest_event_at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.605328Z\"}},{\"id\":\"a-release-leaves-the-build-fleet-on-its-own-once-its-checks-pass-and-nobody-waits-to-start-it\",\"title\":\"A release leaves the build fleet on its own once its checks pass, and nobody waits to start it\",\"description\":\"A release leaves the build fleet when its checks are green, as dispatch://OPS-8 begins to make it, and nobody waits on a person to press a button for it.\\n\\nToday a release waits for someone to read the run, compare it with the last one and start the rollout by hand. Most of that reading is the same every time: the same checks, the same thresholds, the same three dashboards. The work under this priority writes those readings down as checks the release run makes itself, so a release that meets them goes out and one that misses them stops and says which reading it missed.\\n\\nIt is not finished while any release needs a person to start it. It is finished when the last ten releases went out on their own, and the ones that stopped stopped for a reason a person agreed with on reading it. A release that stopped is started again by the change that fixes what it missed, never by a person pressing the button anyway, so the readings stay the only way out of the fleet.\",\"description_tree\":{\"type\":\"doc\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"A release leaves the build fleet when its checks are green, as dispatch://OPS-8 begins to make it, and nobody waits on a person to press a button for it.\"}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Today a release waits for someone to read the run, compare it with the last one and start the rollout by hand. Most of that reading is the same every time: the same checks, the same thresholds, the same three dashboards. The work under this priority writes those readings down as checks the release run makes itself, so a release that meets them goes out and one that misses them stops and says which reading it missed.\"}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"It is not finished while any release needs a person to start it. It is finished when the last ten releases went out on their own, and the ones that stopped stopped for a reason a person agreed with on reading it. A release that stopped is started again by the change that fixes what it missed, never by a person pressing the button anyway, so the readings stay the only way out of the fleet.\"}]}]},\"description_tree_exact\":true,\"owner\":\"The platform controller\",\"rank\":\"W\",\"state\":\"live\",\"made_at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.424746Z\",\"made_by\":{\"kind\":\"user\",\"id\":\"alice\",\"proven\":true},\"work\":{\"by_status\":{\"backlog\":0,\"done\":0,\"icebox\":0,\"in_progress\":1,\"needs_review\":0,\"retro\":0,\"testing\":1,\"todo\":0,\"triage\":1},\"claimed\":0,\"open_asks\":1,\"closed_last_7_days\":0,\"newest_event_at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.619667Z\"}},{\"id\":\"release-notes\",\"title\":\"Release notes\",\"description\":\"The release notes are written as the work lands rather than on the day of the release. Each change that a reader of the notes would notice carries a line for them, written by whoever made the change, in the words a reader uses. The release gathers those lines, orders them by what a reader does first, and leaves out what no reader sees.\\n\\nIt is finished when a release's notes are ready the moment its run is green, and nobody spends the release day reading a month of changes to find out what went into it. A change with no line for its readers says why it needs none.\",\"description_tree\":{\"type\":\"doc\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The release notes are written as the work lands rather than on the day of the release. Each change that a reader of the notes would notice carries a line for them, written by whoever made the change, in the words a reader uses. The release gathers those lines, orders them by what a reader does first, and leaves out what no reader sees.\"}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"It is finished when a release's notes are ready the moment its run is green, and nobody spends the release day reading a month of changes to find out what went into it. A change with no line for its readers says why it needs none.\"}]}]},\"description_tree_exact\":true,\"owner\":\"None named\",\"rank\":\"X\",\"state\":\"live\",\"made_at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.429011Z\",\"made_by\":{\"kind\":\"user\",\"id\":\"alice\",\"proven\":true},\"work\":{\"by_status\":{\"backlog\":0,\"done\":0,\"icebox\":0,\"in_progress\":0,\"needs_review\":1,\"retro\":0,\"testing\":0,\"todo\":0,\"triage\":1},\"claimed\":0,\"open_asks\":0,\"closed_last_7_days\":0,\"newest_event_at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.626334Z\"}},{\"id\":\"a-build-survives-the-replacement-of-the-host-it-runs-on\",\"title\":\"A build survives the replacement of the host it runs on\",\"description\":\"The first step is dispatch://OPS-10. The build fleet runs on hosts that are replaced as a matter of course: an image is built, a host takes it, and the host before it is drained and returned. Today a host that is drained in the middle of a build loses the build, and the build starts again from the beginning on another host.\\n\\nThe work under this priority makes a build survive its host. A build writes what it has done so far where the next host can read it, the drain waits for that write, and the next host starts from it rather than from nothing. It is finished when a week of host replacements costs no build more than the minute its new host takes to start, and the fleet's dashboard shows no build lost to a drain.\",\"description_tree\":{\"type\":\"doc\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The first step is dispatch://OPS-10. The build fleet runs on hosts that are replaced as a matter of course: an image is built, a host takes it, and the host before it is drained and returned. Today a host that is drained in the middle of a build loses the build, and the build starts again from the beginning on another host.\"}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The work under this priority makes a build survive its host. A build writes what it has done so far where the next host can read it, the drain waits for that write, and the next host starts from it rather than from nothing. It is finished when a week of host replacements costs no build more than the minute its new host takes to start, and the fleet's dashboard shows no build lost to a drain.\"}]}]},\"description_tree_exact\":true,\"owner\":\"Release's and Docs' controllers\",\"rank\":\"Y\",\"state\":\"live\",\"made_at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.432419Z\",\"made_by\":{\"kind\":\"user\",\"id\":\"alice\",\"proven\":true},\"work\":{\"by_status\":{\"backlog\":0,\"done\":0,\"icebox\":0,\"in_progress\":1,\"needs_review\":0,\"retro\":0,\"testing\":0,\"todo\":1,\"triage\":0},\"claimed\":0,\"open_asks\":0,\"closed_last_7_days\":0,\"newest_event_at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.639599Z\"}},{\"id\":\"verification-reads-every-change-in-the-same-way\",\"title\":\"Verification reads every change in the same way\",\"description\":\"One record of verification per change.\\n\\nVerification reads every change the same way, whoever made it and however large it is, and says in one place what it found.\\n\\nToday there are four places a change is checked: the unit suites, the browser suites, the review of its plan and the reading of its result. Each reports on its own page, in its own words, and a reader who wants to know whether a change is ready opens all four and puts the answer together themselves. Two of them can disagree, and when they do the reader has no way to tell which one read the newer state of the change.\\n\\nThe work under this priority gives a change one record of its verification. Each check writes its result there, with the commit it read, the command it ran and what it found, and the record says which results are current and which were read from an older commit. A change is ready when every check it names has a current result and each result is a pass, and the record says so in those words.\\n\\nIt also covers what happens when a check is wrong. A check that fails on a change that is right is a defect of the check, and the record keeps the reason a person gave for reading past it, so the next reader sees the same reason rather than the same failure with nothing beside it. A check that passes on a change that is wrong is found by the change that fixes it, and that change names the check, so the record of the check shows it once let a defect through.\\n\\nIt is finished when a reader answers whether a change is ready from one page, in under a minute, without opening a log, and when the four places a change was checked before no longer report anything the record does not already hold. The pages those four places drew stay readable for the changes they recorded, and each one says, at its top, where the record of a newer change is read instead, so a reader who follows an old link is sent to the place that answers.\",\"description_tree\":{\"type\":\"doc\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"One record of verification per change.\"}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Verification reads every change the same way, whoever made it and however large it is, and says in one place what it found.\"}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Today there are four places a change is checked: the unit suites, the browser suites, the review of its plan and the reading of its result. Each reports on its own page, in its own words, and a reader who wants to know whether a change is ready opens all four and puts the answer together themselves. Two of them can disagree, and when they do the reader has no way to tell which one read the newer state of the change.\"}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The work under this priority gives a change one record of its verification. Each check writes its result there, with the commit it read, the command it ran and what it found, and the record says which results are current and which were read from an older commit. A change is ready when every check it names has a current result and each result is a pass, and the record says so in those words.\"}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"It also covers what happens when a check is wrong. A check that fails on a change that is right is a defect of the check, and the record keeps the reason a person gave for reading past it, so the next reader sees the same reason rather than the same failure with nothing beside it. A check that passes on a change that is wrong is found by the change that fixes it, and that change names the check, so the record of the check shows it once let a defect through.\"}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"It is finished when a reader answers whether a change is ready from one page, in under a minute, without opening a log, and when the four places a change was checked before no longer report anything the record does not already hold. The pages those four places drew stay readable for the changes they recorded, and each one says, at its top, where the record of a newer change is read instead, so a reader who follows an old link is sent to the place that answers.\"}]}]},\"description_tree_exact\":true,\"owner\":\"The build fleet's owner\",\"rank\":\"Z\",\"state\":\"live\",\"made_at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.436896Z\",\"made_by\":{\"kind\":\"user\",\"id\":\"alice\",\"proven\":true},\"work\":{\"by_status\":{\"backlog\":1,\"done\":0,\"icebox\":0,\"in_progress\":1,\"needs_review\":0,\"retro\":0,\"testing\":0,\"todo\":0,\"triage\":0},\"claimed\":1,\"open_asks\":0,\"closed_last_7_days\":0,\"newest_event_at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.774093Z\"}},{\"id\":\"docs-search-finds-the-page-a-reader-means\",\"title\":\"Docs search finds the page a reader means\",\"description\":\"A search over the docs site finds the page a reader means, by the words they use for it rather than the words the page was written in. The work is a list of the hundred searches readers made last month that opened no page, each with the page that should have answered it, and a change to the search that makes each of them open that page. It is finished when that list, read again a month later, holds fewer than ten searches.\",\"description_tree\":{\"type\":\"doc\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"A search over the docs site finds the page a reader means, by the words they use for it rather than the words the page was written in. The work is a list of the hundred searches readers made last month that opened no page, each with the page that should have answered it, and a change to the search that makes each of them open that page. It is finished when that list, read again a month later, holds fewer than ten searches.\"}]}]},\"description_tree_exact\":true,\"owner\":\"The docs controller\",\"rank\":\"a\",\"state\":\"live\",\"made_at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.441834Z\",\"made_by\":{\"kind\":\"user\",\"id\":\"alice\",\"proven\":true},\"work\":{\"by_status\":{\"backlog\":0,\"done\":0,\"icebox\":0,\"in_progress\":0,\"needs_review\":0,\"retro\":0,\"testing\":0,\"todo\":1,\"triage\":0},\"claimed\":0,\"open_asks\":0,\"closed_last_7_days\":0,\"newest_event_at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.658514Z\"}},{\"id\":\"a-failing-test-row-is-fixed-never-run-again\",\"title\":\"A failing test row is fixed, never run again\",\"description\":\"Start with dispatch://CORE-21.\\n\\nThe test suites that fail on a change and then pass on the same change, with nothing changed between the two runs, are found and fixed rather than run again until they pass.\\n\\nEach run of the suites records which rows failed and on which commit. A row that fails and then passes on one commit is a flaky row, and it is listed with the runs it failed in. The work under this priority reads that list every week, fixes the row at the top of it, and writes down what made it flaky, so the next row that fails for the same reason is fixed the same way.\",\"description_tree\":{\"type\":\"doc\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Start with dispatch://CORE-21.\"}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The test suites that fail on a change and then pass on the same change, with nothing changed between the two runs, are found and fixed rather than run again until they pass.\"}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Each run of the suites records which rows failed and on which commit. A row that fails and then passes on one commit is a flaky row, and it is listed with the runs it failed in. The work under this priority reads that list every week, fixes the row at the top of it, and writes down what made it flaky, so the next row that fails for the same reason is fixed the same way.\"}]}]},\"description_tree_exact\":true,\"owner\":\"Verification's controller\",\"rank\":\"b\",\"state\":\"live\",\"made_at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.445537Z\",\"made_by\":{\"kind\":\"user\",\"id\":\"alice\",\"proven\":true},\"work\":{\"by_status\":{\"backlog\":0,\"done\":0,\"icebox\":0,\"in_progress\":1,\"needs_review\":0,\"retro\":1,\"testing\":0,\"todo\":0,\"triage\":0},\"claimed\":0,\"open_asks\":0,\"closed_last_7_days\":0,\"newest_event_at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.671526Z\"}},{\"id\":\"patch-within-a-day\",\"title\":\"Patch within a day\",\"description\":\"Every host of the build fleet takes a security patch within a day of its release. Today a patch waits for the next image, which is built weekly, so a host can run for six days with a patch it does not have. The work is a patch run that builds an image the day a patch is released and replaces the hosts with it, one at a time, without losing a build; and a page that lists each host with the newest patch it runs.\\n\\nIt is finished when that page shows no host more than a day behind, for a month.\",\"description_tree\":{\"type\":\"doc\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Every host of the build fleet takes a security patch within a day of its release. Today a patch waits for the next image, which is built weekly, so a host can run for six days with a patch it does not have. The work is a patch run that builds an image the day a patch is released and replaces the hosts with it, one at a time, without losing a build; and a page that lists each host with the newest patch it runs.\"}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"It is finished when that page shows no host more than a day behind, for a month.\"}]}]},\"description_tree_exact\":true,\"owner\":\"The fleet controller\",\"rank\":\"c\",\"state\":\"live\",\"made_at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.448695Z\",\"made_by\":{\"kind\":\"user\",\"id\":\"alice\",\"proven\":true},\"work\":{\"by_status\":{\"backlog\":0,\"done\":0,\"icebox\":0,\"in_progress\":0,\"needs_review\":0,\"retro\":0,\"testing\":1,\"todo\":0,\"triage\":0},\"claimed\":0,\"open_asks\":0,\"closed_last_7_days\":0,\"newest_event_at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.677556Z\"}},{\"id\":\"a-one-sitting-setup\",\"title\":\"A one-sitting setup\",\"description\":\"Nobody asks anybody for anything.\\n\\nA person who opens the product for the first time reaches a working setup in one sitting, without asking anybody for anything.\\n\\nThe work under it is the first page a new reader sees, the one command that starts the stack on their machine, the sample data that command loads, and the short tour that walks them from that data to their own. Each step says what it is waiting on while it waits, and a step that fails says what to do next in the words of the page it failed on. It is finished when five people who have never used the product each reach their own first page in under half an hour, reading nothing but what the product shows them on the way.\",\"description_tree\":{\"type\":\"doc\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Nobody asks anybody for anything.\"}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"A person who opens the product for the first time reaches a working setup in one sitting, without asking anybody for anything.\"}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The work under it is the first page a new reader sees, the one command that starts the stack on their machine, the sample data that command loads, and the short tour that walks them from that data to their own. Each step says what it is waiting on while it waits, and a step that fails says what to do next in the words of the page it failed on. It is finished when five people who have never used the product each reach their own first page in under half an hour, reading nothing but what the product shows them on the way.\"}]}]},\"description_tree_exact\":true,\"owner\":\"Docs and support\",\"rank\":\"d\",\"state\":\"live\",\"made_at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.45198Z\",\"made_by\":{\"kind\":\"user\",\"id\":\"alice\",\"proven\":true},\"work\":{\"by_status\":{\"backlog\":0,\"done\":0,\"icebox\":0,\"in_progress\":0,\"needs_review\":0,\"retro\":0,\"testing\":0,\"todo\":1,\"triage\":0},\"claimed\":0,\"open_asks\":0,\"closed_last_7_days\":0,\"newest_event_at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.684185Z\"}},{\"id\":\"the-cost-of-a-merged-change-falls-each-week-as-the-daily-reading-measures-it\",\"title\":\"The cost of a merged change falls each week, as the daily reading measures it\",\"description\":\"The cost of a merged change is read every day, from what the build fleet and the checks spent on it, and the reading falls from one week to the next.\\n\\nThe work under it is the reading itself, which today is put together by hand once a month; a page that shows it each day with the week before it; and the changes that make it fall, chosen from what the reading shows is most of the cost. The first of those is the browser suite, which every change runs in full although most changes touch none of the pages it reads. A change that touches no page runs the rows that read the pages it touches and no other.\",\"description_tree\":{\"type\":\"doc\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The cost of a merged change is read every day, from what the build fleet and the checks spent on it, and the reading falls from one week to the next.\"}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The work under it is the reading itself, which today is put together by hand once a month; a page that shows it each day with the week before it; and the changes that make it fall, chosen from what the reading shows is most of the cost. The first of those is the browser suite, which every change runs in full although most changes touch none of the pages it reads. A change that touches no page runs the rows that read the pages it touches and no other.\"}]}]},\"description_tree_exact\":true,\"owner\":\"The eval controller\",\"rank\":\"e\",\"state\":\"live\",\"made_at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.455395Z\",\"made_by\":{\"kind\":\"user\",\"id\":\"alice\",\"proven\":true},\"work\":{\"by_status\":{\"backlog\":0,\"done\":0,\"icebox\":0,\"in_progress\":1,\"needs_review\":0,\"retro\":0,\"testing\":0,\"todo\":0,\"triage\":0},\"claimed\":0,\"open_asks\":0,\"closed_last_7_days\":0,\"newest_event_at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.692348Z\"}},{\"id\":\"sessions-resume-where-they-stopped-with-nothing-a-person-typed-into-them-lost\",\"title\":\"Sessions resume where they stopped, with nothing a person typed into them lost\",\"description\":\"dispatch://CORE-24 keeps what a person types. A session that stops, because its host was replaced or its connection dropped, resumes where it stopped, with nothing a person typed into it lost.\\n\\nToday a stopped session starts again from its last saved turn, and whatever the person wrote after that turn is gone. Most of the time that is a sentence or two; once a week or so it is a long message written over several minutes, and the person writes it again from memory. The work under this priority keeps what a person types where the session's next host can read it, as they type it, and the next host offers it back to them the moment the session resumes.\\n\\nIt is finished when a month of host replacements and dropped connections loses no word anybody typed, and when the page that resumes a session says it did so in one line rather than leaving the person to notice that nothing changed.\",\"description_tree\":{\"type\":\"doc\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"dispatch://CORE-24 keeps what a person types. A session that stops, because its host was replaced or its connection dropped, resumes where it stopped, with nothing a person typed into it lost.\"}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Today a stopped session starts again from its last saved turn, and whatever the person wrote after that turn is gone. Most of the time that is a sentence or two; once a week or so it is a long message written over several minutes, and the person writes it again from memory. The work under this priority keeps what a person types where the session's next host can read it, as they type it, and the next host offers it back to them the moment the session resumes.\"}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"It is finished when a month of host replacements and dropped connections loses no word anybody typed, and when the page that resumes a session says it did so in one line rather than leaving the person to notice that nothing changed.\"}]}]},\"description_tree_exact\":true,\"owner\":\"None named\",\"rank\":\"f\",\"state\":\"live\",\"made_at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.45933Z\",\"made_by\":{\"kind\":\"user\",\"id\":\"alice\",\"proven\":true},\"work\":{\"by_status\":{\"backlog\":0,\"done\":0,\"icebox\":0,\"in_progress\":0,\"needs_review\":1,\"retro\":0,\"testing\":0,\"todo\":0,\"triage\":0},\"claimed\":0,\"open_asks\":0,\"closed_last_7_days\":0,\"newest_event_at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.699805Z\"}},{\"id\":\"every-page-answers-in-under-a-second-at-the-load-we-are-heading-to\",\"title\":\"Every page answers in under a second at the load we are heading to\",\"description\":\"Every page a reader opens answers in under a second, at the load the product is heading to rather than the load it has today.\\n\\nThe work under this priority is a load run that opens each page the way a reader does, at ten times today's traffic, and records how long each one took to answer; a list of the pages that took longer than a second, slowest first; and a change for each page on that list that brings it under. The run is part of every release, so a change that makes a page slower stops the release that carries it and names the page.\\n\\nIt is finished when the run's list is empty for three releases in a row, and when the slowest page of each run is shown on the release's own page beside its checks, so a reader of the release sees how near the bound the slowest page stood.\",\"description_tree\":{\"type\":\"doc\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Every page a reader opens answers in under a second, at the load the product is heading to rather than the load it has today.\"}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The work under this priority is a load run that opens each page the way a reader does, at ten times today's traffic, and records how long each one took to answer; a list of the pages that took longer than a second, slowest first; and a change for each page on that list that brings it under. The run is part of every release, so a change that makes a page slower stops the release that carries it and names the page.\"}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"It is finished when the run's list is empty for three releases in a row, and when the slowest page of each run is shown on the release's own page beside its checks, so a reader of the release sees how near the bound the slowest page stood.\"}]}]},\"description_tree_exact\":true,\"owner\":\"The release team\",\"rank\":\"g\",\"state\":\"live\",\"made_at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.463192Z\",\"made_by\":{\"kind\":\"user\",\"id\":\"alice\",\"proven\":true},\"work\":{\"by_status\":{\"backlog\":0,\"done\":0,\"icebox\":0,\"in_progress\":0,\"needs_review\":0,\"retro\":0,\"testing\":0,\"todo\":0,\"triage\":1},\"claimed\":0,\"open_asks\":0,\"closed_last_7_days\":0,\"newest_event_at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.707519Z\"}},{\"id\":\"every-surface-of-dispatch-reads-at-every-width-from-a-phone-to-a-wide-screen\",\"title\":\"Every surface of Dispatch reads at every width from a phone to a wide screen\",\"description\":\"\",\"owner\":\"alice\",\"rank\":\"h\",\"state\":\"live\",\"made_at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:10.128266Z\",\"made_by\":{\"kind\":\"user\",\"id\":\"alice\",\"proven\":true},\"work\":{\"by_status\":{\"backlog\":0,\"done\":0,\"icebox\":0,\"in_progress\":3,\"needs_review\":0,\"retro\":0,\"testing\":0,\"todo\":2,\"triage\":1},\"claimed\":1,\"open_asks\":1,\"closed_last_7_days\":0,\"newest_event_at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:10.669378Z\"}}],\"work_under_no_priority\":{\"count\":6,\"by_project\":{\"CORE\":3,\"OPS\":3},\"issues\":[{\"key\":\"OPS-15\",\"title\":\"A build host drained for replacement while a verification run still holds it waits for the run to write the last check it finished, then hands the run to the next host with its record, its cache key and the list of checks it has still to run, and the next host picks the run up from that list rather than from the first check; the run's own page says which host read which checks, how long the hand-over took and whether any check was read twice, a run that could not be handed over says why in one line at the top of that page, beside a link to the drained host's own log, and the fleet's dashboard counts the runs handed over each day beside the runs that started again from nothing, so the people who replace hosts can see what a replacement still costs\",\"project\":\"OPS\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"assignee\":\"alice\",\"claim\":{\"actor\":{\"kind\":\"session\",\"id\":\"019a1c07-6d4b-7e80-bf39-4a1b5c8d9e07\",\"origin\":{\"session_title\":\"🛠️ FIX: Keep the build cache warm when a runner restarts\"}},\"at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.785565Z\"},\"changed_at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.785565Z\",\"advances\":[],\"moved_at\":null,\"moved_by\":null},{\"key\":\"OPS-3\",\"title\":\"A machine that misses three heartbeats in a row is listed as unresponsive rather than gone, with the moment it was last seen and the issue it was working on then\",\"project\":\"OPS\",\"status\":\"retro\",\"assignee\":\"alice\",\"claim\":{\"actor\":{\"kind\":\"session\",\"id\":\"019a1c08-7e5c-7f91-8a4a-5b2c6d9e0f08\",\"origin\":{\"session_title\":\"019a1c08-7e5c-7f91-8a4a-5b2c6d9e0f08\"}},\"at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.749186Z\"},\"changed_at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.749186Z\",\"advances\":[],\"moved_at\":null,\"moved_by\":null},{\"key\":\"CORE-9\",\"title\":\"The Inbox count on the rail settles within a second of a reply being read on another device, and never counts one reply twice while the read that clears it is still in flight on a slow link\",\"project\":\"CORE\",\"status\":\"needs_review\",\"assignee\":\"alice\",\"claim\":{\"actor\":{\"kind\":\"session\",\"id\":\"019a1c03-2f0d-7c4c-ab85-0c7d1e4f5a03\",\"origin\":{\"session_title\":\"Reviewer\"}},\"at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.738419Z\"},\"changed_at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.738419Z\",\"advances\":[],\"moved_at\":null,\"moved_by\":null},{\"key\":\"OPS-2\",\"title\":\"Rotating the agent token on a build host restarts no session that holds a claim, and a session that loses its connection during the rotation reconnects on its own\",\"project\":\"OPS\",\"status\":\"testing\",\"assignee\":\"alice\",\"claim\":{\"actor\":{\"kind\":\"session\",\"id\":\"019a1c02-1e9c-7b3b-9f74-3b6c0d3e4f02\",\"origin\":{\"session_title\":\"Tester\"}},\"at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.733212Z\"},\"changed_at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.733212Z\",\"advances\":[],\"moved_at\":null,\"moved_by\":null},{\"key\":\"CORE-8\",\"title\":\"The broadcast composer keeps each recipient's place in the send order when the list it was picked from refreshes under the sender\",\"project\":\"CORE\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"assignee\":\"alice\",\"claim\":{\"actor\":{\"kind\":\"session\",\"id\":\"019a1c01-0d7b-7a2a-8e93-4a5b6c7d8e01\",\"origin\":{\"session_title\":\"Planner\"}},\"at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.728041Z\"},\"changed_at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.728041Z\",\"advances\":[],\"moved_at\":null,\"moved_by\":null},{\"key\":\"CORE-3\",\"title\":\"Broadcast recipients keep their send order\",\"project\":\"CORE\",\"status\":\"needs_review\",\"assignee\":\"alice\",\"claim\":null,\"changed_at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:07.159952Z\",\"advances\":[],\"moved_at\":null,\"moved_by\":null}]},\"priority_work_parked\":{\"count\":3,\"by_priority\":{\"every-change-that-reaches-the-build-fleet-is-verified-before-a-person-reads-it\":2,\"verification-reads-every-change-in-the-same-way\":1},\"issues\":[{\"key\":\"CORE-19\",\"title\":\"Fold the unit suites' and the browser suites' reports into the one record a change keeps, and retire the two pages that drew them\",\"project\":\"CORE\",\"status\":\"backlog\",\"assignee\":\"alice\",\"claim\":{\"actor\":{\"kind\":\"session\",\"id\":\"019a1c07-6d4b-7e80-bf39-4a1b5c8d9e07\",\"origin\":{\"session_title\":\"🛠️ FIX: Keep the build cache warm when a runner restarts\"}},\"at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.774093Z\"},\"changed_at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.774093Z\",\"advances\":[{\"id\":\"verification-reads-every-change-in-the-same-way\",\"inherited\":false}],\"moved_at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.651269Z\",\"moved_by\":{\"kind\":\"user\",\"id\":\"alice\",\"proven\":true}},{\"key\":\"CORE-16\",\"title\":\"Show a change's verification record in the margin of its pull request, beside the lines each of its checks read\",\"project\":\"CORE\",\"status\":\"icebox\",\"assignee\":\"alice\",\"claim\":null,\"changed_at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.599542Z\",\"advances\":[{\"id\":\"every-change-that-reaches-the-build-fleet-is-verified-before-a-person-reads-it\",\"inherited\":false}],\"moved_at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.597187Z\",\"moved_by\":{\"kind\":\"user\",\"id\":\"alice\",\"proven\":true}},{\"key\":\"CORE-5\",\"title\":\"Agents page freshness folds\",\"project\":\"CORE\",\"status\":\"backlog\",\"assignee\":\"alice\",\"claim\":null,\"changed_at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:09.476066Z\",\"advances\":[{\"id\":\"every-change-that-reaches-the-build-fleet-is-verified-before-a-person-reads-it\",\"inherited\":false}],\"moved_at\":\"2026-11-27T11:26:06.585247Z\",\"moved_by\":{\"kind\":\"user\",\"id\":\"alice\",\"proven\":true}}]}}\n"
